---
TDL: 0.2
Shell: 0.1
Name: Volume_OSD
---

# The volume on-screen display (M7h): what a Panel shows for a moment when the default output's
# volume or mute changes: an icon, the output's name, a bar and the percent, or "Muted". The module
# follows the sound server itself (ctx.audio, as the Audio module does; no Audio use is needed).
# It shows nothing at start, for the first reading of the server, for a change of the default
# output (the new output is the baseline) or for a change of the microphone or the list of
# outputs. On a volume or mute change it shows the Panel that holds it (ctx.surface.show) and the
# Panel hides itself `duration` milliseconds after the last change; a change in that time starts
# the time again. It says nothing aloud: the Audio module's `announce` does that (so it is not
# said twice) and the Panel never takes the keyboard.
#
# Put it in a Panel that starts hidden, is click-through and has no keyboard, on the overlay
# layer (the guide's example):
#
#   Panel { Name: Volume_Panel, Layer: OVERLAY, Keyboard: NONE, Input_Region: [], Visible: false,
#           Anchor: [BOTTOM], Inset: [0, 0, 0, 80], Width: 300, Height: 64,
#           Style { Background: $color.surface_raised, Corner_Radius: 12, Elevation: 20% },
#           Children { Volume_OSD { } } }
#
# The Python sends `ready`, `volume`, `bar` (the volume held to 0 to 100), `volume_text`
# ("45 %"), `readout` (the volume text, or "Muted"), `muted`, `icon`, `name` (the output) and
# `label` (the accessible name). Muted is shown by the icon's shape, by the word and by the bar
# drawn dimmed: never by colour alone.
#
# Accessibility: the module is a GROUP named "Volume, <output>, <45 %|muted>" that holds a
# PROGRESSBAR named "Volume"; the icon and the two texts are hidden from assistive technology (the
# group's name says them). There is no live region: nothing is announced by the module.
Module {
    Style: Volume_OSD_Style.tdl

    Params {
        # milliseconds the Panel stays after the last change
        duration { Type: number, Default: 1500 }
        # the output's name above the bar
        show_name { Type: boolean, Default: true }
    }

    FlexBox {
        Name: Root
        Width: 100%
        Height: 100%
        Role: GROUP
        Label: <| label |>
        Flex: HORIZONTAL
        Align_Items: CENTER
        Spacing: <| space.step_4 |>
        Padding: <| [space.step_5, space.step_3, space.step_5, space.step_3] |>
        Children {
            SVG {
                Name: Glyph
                Icon: <| icon |>
                Width: 24
                Height: 24
                A11y_Hidden: true
            }
            FlexBox {
                Name: Body
                Flex: VERTICAL
                Flex_Grow: 1
                Justify_Content: CENTER
                Spacing: 6
                Children {
                    If <| params.show_name |> {
                        Text {
                            Name: Output
                            Class: osd_name
                            Text: <| name |>
                            Wrap: NONE
                            Width: 100%
                            Height: AUTO
                            A11y_Hidden: true
                        }
                    }
                    ProgressBar {
                        Name: Bar
                        Label: "Volume"
                        Value: <| bar |>
                        Max: 100
                        Width: 100%
                        Opacity: <| 0.4 if muted else 1 |>
                    }
                }
            }
            Text {
                Name: Value
                Class: osd_value
                Text: <| readout |>
                Wrap: NONE
                Width: 64
                Height: AUTO
                Text_Align: END
                A11y_Hidden: true
            }
        }
    }
}
